    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What happened to Charlie? You will need courage to find the answer to this question.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Immerse yourself in this first-person psychological horror, where every choice matters in a non-linear narrative. Face the memories and demons of Charlie's past, but are they really demons? And, above all, do you really have to face them? Not doing so is also an option, but know that every choice has a consequence. Even not acting. Even not solving the environmental puzzles will lead you to the ending you deserve.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556490/extras/ba6464516ef57184ffbb48f591fe986c.avif?t=1750298633\" width=800 height=442 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Will you trust the flying brain, a seemingly friendly figure, or the mysterious voice, a seemingly hostile figure? What is the right thing to do? What do you really want? A happy ending? These and other questions will only be answered if we have the courage to ask them and listen to the answers.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Features:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A dark environment that reflects Charlie's state of mind</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Multiple choices that will lead to one of three endings, or to a senseless game over</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Brain or voice? Rationality or feelings? How much should we use these two parts?</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Traumatic Memories We Can Face or Run Away From</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Did Charlie Really Do Wrong? Charlie's fate Is in Your Hands</p></li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >What happened to Charlie? You will need courage to find the answer to this question.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Immerse yourself in this first-person psychological horror, where every choice matters in a non-linear narrative. Face the memories and demons of Charlie's past, but are they really demons? And, above all, do you really have to face them? Not doing so is also an option, but know that every choice has a consequence. Even not acting. Even not solving the environmental puzzles will lead you to the ending you deserve.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3556490/extras/ba6464516ef57184ffbb48f591fe986c.avif?t=1750298633\" width=800 height=442 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Will you trust the flying brain, a seemingly friendly figure, or the mysterious voice, a seemingly hostile figure? What is the right thing to do? What do you really want? A happy ending? These and other questions will only be answered if we have the courage to ask them and listen to the answers.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Features:</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A dark environment that reflects Charlie's state of mind</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Multiple choices that will lead to one of three endings, or to a senseless game over</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Brain or voice? Rationality or feelings? How much should we use these two parts?</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Traumatic Memories We Can Face or Run Away From</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Did Charlie Really Do Wrong? Charlie's fate Is in Your Hands</p></li></ul>",
    "short_description": "A psychological horror where Charlie will have to deal with his memories and his demons... but are they really demons? Who can Charlie trust? The flying brain or the mysterious voice? Every choice matters and will lead you to a different ending",
